Stage 5b: the content sets on the FLOOR transcoder (arm b), same machine.

This is the sharp version of the arm b question. Arm b measured 0.93 to 1.04 of
arm a on ASCII, where a narrowing transcoder has nothing to do -- so that result
is nearly a measurement of nothing. The floor's transcoder is a DIFFERENT
overload (Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(char*, int, byte*, int) against
Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(ReadOnlySpan<char>, Span<byte>)), and if the two ever
diverge it is where the transcoder has real work. Compare with
stage5-content-sets.log, which is the same table for arm a.

commit:  d281acf6ae3d78510d62c68f969ff16fe52e0768 (+ this slice)

